# Intent: the ring is dark and the eyes are shut when the power key switches the unit off (owner, 2026-11-13). The PMIC cuts power with no warning about 4 s after the key goes down (register 0x27, the shortest setting) and the ring keeps its last colours (patch 050 header). The long-press flag comes at about 1 s: register 0x41 bit 2 makes the PMIC keep it in register 0x49, the touch timer reads it every 100 ms, clears it, blanks the ring (the host's colours stay in the shadow) and sets the sleeping face. A key let go before the cut puts the ring (only if this handler blanked it) and the neutral face back 6 s after the flag. Short presses do nothing. The register and bit meanings are from the AXP2101 register map and are not yet checked on a unit.
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan.cc, hal/hal_io_expander.cpp, hal/board/hal_bridge.h (MIT). Applies after 113.
# Check after a flash (10 minutes, on USB and on battery): hold the power button: after about a second the log says "power key held", the ring goes dark and the face shuts its eyes; at about 4 s the unit switches off with the ring dark. A press under a second: nothing. Let go at 2 s: the face and the ring come back about 6 s after the hold was seen. Does the unit stay off on USB, and is the ring dark?
